{"name":"Pericallis Hybrida","hex":"#904fef","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Pericallis × hybrida","blocks":[{"text":"Pericallis × hybrida, known as cineraria, florist's cineraria or common ragwort is a flowering plant in the family Asteraceae. It originated as a hybrid between Pericallis cruenta and P. lanata, both natives of the Canary Islands. The hybrid was first developed in the British royal gardens in 1777. It was originally known as Cineraria × hybrida, but the genus Cineraria is now restricted to a group of South African species, with the Canary Island species being transferred to the genus Pericallis; some botanists also treat it in a broad view of the large and widespread genus Senecio. Some varieties are sold under the trade name Senetti."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Red_Cineraria_Pericallis_2.jpg/330px-Red_Cineraria_Pericallis_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pericallis_%C3%97_hybrida","wikidata":"Q1494593"},{"title":"Pericallis","blocks":[{"text":"Pericallis is a small genus of 15 species of flowering plants in the family Asteraceae, native to the Canary Islands, Madeira and Azores. The genus includes herbaceous plants and small subshrubs. In the past, the genus was often included in either Cineraria or Senecio."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Pericallis_cruenta1.jpg/330px-Pericallis_cruenta1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pericallis","wikidata":"Q2709984"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Red_Cineraria_Pericallis_2.jpg/500px-Red_Cineraria_Pericallis_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Red_Cineraria_Pericallis_2.jpg/1280px-Red_Cineraria_Pericallis_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Red_Cineraria_Pericallis_2.jpg/500px-Red_Cineraria_Pericallis_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_Cineraria_Pericallis_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Pericallis_%C3%97_hybrida_%282058070328%29.jpg/500px-Pericallis_%C3%97_hybrida_%282058070328%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Pericallis_%C3%97_hybrida_%282058070328%29.jpg/500px-Pericallis_%C3%97_hybrida_%282058070328%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blue cineraria","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APericallis_%C3%97_hybrida_(2058070328).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Pericallis_cruenta1.jpg/500px-Pericallis_cruenta1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Pericallis_cruenta1.jpg/500px-Pericallis_cruenta1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APericallis_cruenta1.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}